{
  "$comment": "THE one place for colours. Every site, Storybook, authentik's pages and every email is generated from this file. After editing it run `npm run palette` in SharedUI: it rewrites palette.css, src/lib/palette.ts and brand/logo.svg here, and fails if a text pair is below WCAG AA. Infrastructure's authentik image downloads this file and brand/logo.svg from a tagged SharedUI release (its SHAREDUI_REF), so nothing is copied between repos. Each colour has a light and a dark value (the same twice when it doesn't change with the theme) and `use`, which Storybook shows. `choices` are the colours visitors can pick for each of the three brand roles (ColourPicker): the first of each is the default and uses the Brand values above; the others override every token of that role (e.g. primary, primary-hover, primary-soft, primary-ink, on-primary), with the same light/dark rules. `presets` are named combinations of one choice per role; the first is the default.",
